prop("N001","There is A=A(T,gamma,R)<infinity such that every real mean-zero datum a0 in H^gamma(Torus) with ||a0||_(H^gamma)<=R has a unique real mean-zero exact KdV solution u in C([0,T];H^gamma), obtained by smooth approximation, satisfying sup_[0,T]||u(t)||_(H^gamma)<=A. Smooth data have smooth solutions. If a0,b0 are two such data then sup_[0,T]||u_a0(t)-u_b0(t)||_2<=K(T,2*R)||a0-b0||_2. The same estimate holds for any two real mean-zero L^2 data with sum of norms <=2*R. Twisting v(t)=S_(-t)u(t) preserves these bounds; for smooth data v'=(1/2)B_t(v,v). Thus M=1+sup_[0,T]||v(t)||_(H^gamma)<=1+A uniformly on the original ball.",
[b("a0","periodic distribution"),b("b0","periodic distribution"),b("u","exact solution associated to a0"),b("u_a0","exact solution associated to a0"),b("u_b0","exact solution associated to b0"),b("v","twisted exact solution"),b("A","uniform nonnegative real bound"),b("K","positive real Lipschitz constant"),b("M","positive real bound")],
